From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:40:20 -0400
Subject: make the Arc metrics tunable without a rebuild

Matching a reference screenshot means trying a number, looking at the result,
and trying another. As constants, each of those attempts cost a compile and a
link. As feature parameters they cost nothing:

  tooling/capture-ui --features \
    'SteddingArcStyleWindow:contents_corner_radius/28/vertical_tab_height/64'

Verified: that command produces 64 pt tab rows and a visibly larger corner
against a build that was already made, with no rebuild.

The contents corner radius, the vertical tab row height and the tab pill radius
now come from stedding::kArcStyleWindow parameters, declared in one small
source_set that depends only on //base so layout_constants can use it without
pulling in views. Defaults are unchanged and remain the shipping values from
docs/UI-SPEC.md; the override path exists for iteration and nothing in the
product depends on it.

The sidebar width is deliberately not a parameter. It is already resizable and
pref-backed at runtime, so a second knob would only be a way to disagree with
the pref.

Why: the iteration loop for a pixel match is look-change-look, and a build in
the middle of it is the whole cost.
Removable when: the metrics stop moving, at which point they can go back to
being constants.
